+# UI 006 — one object, several questions
+
+23 November 2026. Owner: UI, `ui/visual-laboratory`. Recorded before implementation.
+Baseline: `dcc8d8e`. The operator explicitly assigns this lane from the research
+session. Only `config/environment.json` was dirty; its SHA-256 is
+`f14595ffd2f9fb435094f780dbbb9b2625c6ad47eface83ce3d838f70a6d647b`.
+Setup owns that change. No Engine work, launch configuration, publication or new
+model session is included.
+
+## Decision and alternatives
+
+Retain the opening markup, typography, media controller and original assets.
+Use a single persistent, code-drawn module schematic beside the active interior
+reading surface. Selection changes emphasis; interface detail exposes a separate
+relationship diagram; interrupted state leaves the scene unchanged and presents
+the two possibilities in the pinned fixture. No mechanical animation is justified.
+The scene is an explanatory arrangement, not a reconstruction of the film or CAD.
+Native scroll carries long text and small-screen reading. It is never a slide deck.
+
+Use instantaneous, synchronous state commits first. No View Transition, WebGL,
+blur, glass or animation is needed for this slice. Opaque near-black material is
+the legibility and low-power baseline, including when filters are unsupported.
+Reject full-document transitions (previous flashing), a second renderer (no
+qualified geometry), and photographic part hotspots (would assert unverified
+correspondence). A future scoped transition must beat this instant path in measured
+use; support alone is not a reason to add it.
+
+URL path and allowlisted query parameters own view, part, interface disclosure
+and evidence selection. Native links carry these states; one commit function
+updates the scene, content, metadata and focus. Back restores the previous state
+and its focus/reading position; Escape follows the containing view. Existing
+legacy hashes and eight static routes remain. No asynchronous reveal can commit
+a stale selection. Fixture arrival only fills provenance and fixture fields.
+
+## Evidence and source boundary
+
+Frozen v1: `2a4083ac15e64fbf3f6f57355827efd5d2ff0a7a`; fixture hash
+`b231fa24f057ce647dbf282ed8233fc88d0bbbed579995213306edac30e65d44`.
+At synthetic t=1, `lock_ack=received` is stale (sampled 0, received 1, epoch 0).
+The two authored candidates differ only in host `partial`/`locked`. Do not turn
+these into probabilities, validated physical possibilities or release advice.
+The fixture expressly requires mechanism review for reachability. Author-assigned
+truth is kept separate from observations. Outcomes are unmeasured, geometry is
+missing, and physical limits remain unknown. Electrical isolation has no measured
+voltage trace in this fixture; show that missing evidence, not invented readings.
+
+Read v3 and the existing UI decisions/receipts. This task does not repeat the
+historical PDF or underlying scientific methods audit and imports no new science.
+The visual reference review is in `interior-reference-review-2026-11-23.md`.
+
+## Bound and rejection criteria
+
+Serial local work only; no dependency installation, paid job or external write.
+Keep the public package below its existing 31 MiB bound. No new scene request on
+opening paint; use inline SVG and defer the pinned fixture until inspection.
+Keep original media/controller bytes. Compare baseline and candidate packages
+and browser measurements where available; DOM timing is not device performance.
+
+Reject if state/URL/focus disagree, quick reselection revives an old state, the
+schematic implies a measured mechanism, missing data becomes zero, the hero
+changes, no-JS routes lose their explanation, or private files enter the package.
+Verify Node, DOM, contract negative controls, package and preservation checks.
+Browser bridge is unavailable; native Chrome briefly rendered the baseline hero,
+then failed twice with `Sky Computer Use native pipe startup failed`. Keep all
+unexecuted browser/device/accessibility/performance checks explicit. A local
+candidate is deliverable; browser acceptance cannot be claimed from source tests.
