+# Interior references — inspected 23 November 2026
+
+Read-only source inspection; no sibling bootstrap, build, modification or engine
+import. These are actual implementations, not invented screenshots. Live approval
+or identity beyond the identified source revision is not inferred.
+
+| Reference and inspected source | Useful interaction | Do not copy | CARTAN consequence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Reiyah Console `1ca96a94f8a0da9abba1b4903eca1d6949595342`, `src/App.tsx`, `lib/urlstate.ts`, `stations/Ledger.tsx`, `README.md` | Current DOM survives while a destination loads; only the latest request can commit. URL selection identifies the evidence artifact. | Idle ledger cursor and fixed one-page/no-scroll assumption. Its verified artifact skyline is not module geometry. | Keep one scene node, synchronous selection and a readable return path; allow long text to scroll. |
+| Sentinel site in portfolio `2de873bdf657e93234873dd022649b8e3565a7b8`, `src/app/sentinel/page.tsx`, `components/research-products/SentinelDecisionArc.tsx`, `ResearchProductInstrument.tsx` | The selected exact trace frame supplies the same values to the visual and spoken description; unavailable readings remain unavailable. Source commit, evidence feed and integrity sidecar have explicit links. | Timeline interpolation, risk-field atmosphere, metric/tape density. CARTAN has no equivalent measured trace. | Pin the fixture, label its synthetic time, keep the scene still, link its exact bytes and show unknowns beside the question. |
+| Nisayon UI `ec909e81a6e2afd1671d59e0ff1bdb9a66a273f9`, `apps/instrument/src/state/studyRoute.ts`, `ui/EvidenceFlow.tsx`; prior UI 005 inspected focus/opening at `808e750` | A study URL retains its generation identity, selected trial and item; invalid state is rejected rather than guessed. Reading preserves an anchor across reflow. | Column/page navigation and fixed-workspace reading modes. The user's CARTAN instruction explicitly rejects them. | Serialize part, interface and record selection; keep ordinary overflow/reflow and a single DOM for keyboard/touch. |
+
+Sentinel's verified local routing maps `sentinel.danielwahnich.dev` to `/sentinel`.
+The live URL failed retrieval through the web tool. Reiyah and Nisayon were
+inspected as local implementations, not claimed as live screenshot reviews.
+The separate Sentinel research repository at `20fefa9` is not the site renderer.
+
+## Browser and accessibility sources
+
+Reviewed the primary specifications and vendor documentation:
+
+- [CSS View Transitions Level 1](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-view-transitions-1/):
+  document snapshots do not establish support for scoped element transitions.
+- [Chrome element-scoped transitions](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/css-ui/view-transitions/element-scoped-view-transitions/),
+  published 27 March 2026, describes Chrome 147+ and element-level scopes.
+- [WebKit Safari 18 features](https://webkit.org/blog/15865/webkit-features-in-safari-18-0/)
+  documents View Transitions and unprefixed backdrop filtering; it is not evidence
+  that the installed Safari supports element-scoped transitions.
+- [Filter Effects Level 2](https://www.w3.org/TR/filter-effects-2/): filtering is an
+  optional rendering effect. CARTAN's text uses an opaque surface without it.
+- [WCAG 2.2](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/): review reflow, contrast, visible and
+  unobscured focus, keyboard access and target sizes; no conformance certification
+  follows from source or DOM checks.
+- [WAI modal dialog pattern](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/dialog-modal/):
+  focus enters the existing native film dialog, Escape dismisses, and focus returns
+  to its opener. The interior is not modal and must not trap focus.
+
+Machine: MacBookPro18,1, Apple M1 Pro, 16 GiB, macOS 14.4 (23E214).
+Running Chrome binary: 157.0.8103.51. Native baseline hero rendering was observed;
+phone layouts, runtime feature detection, Safari and VoiceOver remain pending
+after both browser access routes failed. Vendor support statements are distinct
+from tested browser support. No browser flags or global preferences were changed.
